00:14:20,730 --> 00:14:22,910
They become trainees, right?

277
00:14:23,790 --> 00:14:24,330
But,

278
00:14:24,330 --> 00:14:25,410
Luke...

279
00:14:25,410 --> 00:14:26,990
At 19 years old,

280
00:14:26,990 --> 00:14:28,370
That belt...

281
00:14:28,370 --> 00:14:29,470
Oh, wait, my bad.

282
00:14:29,470 --> 00:14:31,330
He met Ben Kenobi,

283
00:14:31,330 --> 00:14:32,570
And at 19,

284
00:14:32,570 --> 00:14:34,550
He learned about the Force for the first time, right?

285
00:14:34,550 --> 00:14:35,570
Right?

286
00:14:35,570 --> 00:14:38,670
That's why he's so strong.

287
00:14:38,670 --> 00:14:44,930
And even Anakin Skywalker was... 9? Around 9 years old, right?

288
00:14:44,930 --> 00:14:48,810
Even at 9, everyone was like, 'He's too late!'

289
00:14:48,810 --> 00:14:51,710
But then you've got Luke at 19!

290
00:14:51,710 --> 00:14:56,370
You can really tell he has Anakin Skywalker's blood in him.

291
00:14:56,370 --> 00:14:58,930
That's how I see it.

292
00:14:58,930 --> 00:15:01,630
That's why he must be so strong, really.

293
00:15:03,030 --> 00:15:03,690
Exactly.

294
00:15:03,690 --> 00:15:07,550
1, 2, 3, ..., 6.

295
00:15:07,550 --> 00:15:08,290
Six stickers.

296
00:15:08,290 --> 00:15:10,150
First, the chocolate...

297
00:15:10,150 --> 00:15:11,170
Pure talent.

298
00:15:11,170 --> 00:15:12,330
He's truly talented.

299
00:15:12,330 --> 00:15:15,730
Luke Skywalker, who has nothing but raw talent...

300
00:15:15,730 --> 00:15:16,490
Why...

301
00:15:16,490 --> 00:15:18,450
Why...

302
00:15:18,450 --> 00:15:20,910
Did he end up like that?

303
00:15:20,910 --> 00:15:27,470
Didn't she recently visit Tokyo?

304
00:15:27,470 --> 00:15:28,370
Fennec.

305
00:15:28,370 --> 00:15:29,790
I wanted to meet her.

306
00:15:29,790 --> 00:15:30,830
When are you...

307
00:15:30,830 --> 00:15:33,710
Coming to Star Wars Celebration?

308
00:15:33,710 --> 00:15:35,040
Hey!

309
00:15:35,040 --> 00:15:40,010
Please come to Comic-Con or something. I want to meet Fennec Shand!

310
00:15:40,010 --> 00:15:49,970
A skilled human female assassin and mercenary. She's worked for many crime syndicates, like the Hutt Syndicate.

311
00:15:49,970 --> 00:15:55,930
So cute. Fennec is great. I really love Fennec Shand.

312
00:15:55,930 --> 00:16:02,310
Nice. I love strong women.

313
00:16:02,310 --> 00:16:05,310
I really love Big Sister Fennec.

314
00:16:05,310 --> 00:16:07,110
I'll clean up here later.

315
00:16:07,910 --> 00:16:11,910
Apparently, she recently came to visit Tokyo Disneyland.

316
00:16:11,910 --> 00:16:13,710
Big Sister Fennec did.

317
00:16:13,710 --> 00:16:15,510
Man...

318
00:16:15,510 --> 00:16:18,510
But even though Korone loves her, I'm not sure I'd notice her.

319
00:16:18,510 --> 00:16:21,510
Because when I'm walking, I hardly look at other people.

320
00:16:22,310 --> 00:16:23,310
I wouldn't even notice her!

321
00:16:23,310 --> 00:16:26,110
But I bet their aura is just different.

322
00:16:28,380 --> 00:16:30,380
Like, since they took photos with the Mandalorian and everyone...

323
00:16:30,380 --> 00:16:32,900
Since they took photos, maybe they went to a pop-up store too.

324
00:16:32,900 --> 00:16:35,540
Alright, give me the chocolate!

325
00:16:35,540 --> 00:16:38,860
I don't even look at their faces.

326
00:16:38,860 --> 00:16:41,780
It's all about the style, for sure.

327
00:16:42,630 --> 00:16:43,700
Pop!

328
00:16:46,200 --> 00:16:47,780
This is the movie title.

329
00:16:47,780 --> 00:16:49,560
The Mandalorian & Grogu.

330
00:16:49,560 --> 00:16:51,400
The Mandalorian & Goo-goo.

331
00:16:51,400 --> 00:16:55,180
Grogu looks like a melon pan, so cute.

332
00:16:55,180 --> 00:16:56,380
Here it is.

333
00:16:58,580 --> 00:17:02,200
"What is the description for The Mandalorian & Grogu?"

334
00:17:02,740 --> 00:17:10,160
"Grogu is a special child targeted by the remnants of the Empire. The Mandalorian protects him and they set off on an adventure."

335
00:17:10,160 --> 00:17:14,800
I mean, the fact that Grogu's name is Grogu is kind of a spoiler in itself.

336
00:17:14,900 --> 00:17:17,480
Well, by now, it's movie time.

337
00:17:17,480 --> 00:17:20,380
"Congrats, Grogu! You're not 'The Child' anymore, right?"

338
00:17:20,380 --> 00:17:23,250
"I'm Grogu! I am Grogu!"

339
00:17:25,240 --> 00:17:27,650
He really loves his Pa, right?

340
00:17:27,650 --> 00:17:28,740
Nice.

341
00:17:29,120 --> 00:17:30,140
So cute.

342
00:17:30,140 --> 00:17:32,140
He's basically shaped like a melon pan.

343
00:17:33,540 --> 00:17:36,660
Now, let me see... uh...

344
00:17:36,660 --> 00:17:39,840
You know, this Mandalorian movie—or show...

345
00:17:39,840 --> 00:17:42,380
Wait, was it like... stuffed animals?

346
00:17:42,500 --> 00:17:45,320
What was it called again?

347
00:17:45,400 --> 00:17:48,960
It was almost like Child's Play...

348
00:17:48,960 --> 00:17:50,780
It was like a puppet show!

349
00:17:50,850 --> 00:17:52,780
It's amazing, really.

350
00:17:53,390 --> 00:17:56,560
Like when the... Angelan? Andalusia? was attacked.

351
00:17:56,560 --> 00:17:57,420
Seriously, that...

352
00:17:57,420 --> 00:17:59,960
It felt like I was watching Child's Play.

353
00:17:59,960 --> 00:18:00,520
That's the memory.

354
00:18:00,520 --> 00:18:01,520
Puppet, puppet.

355
00:18:01,520 --> 00:18:04,980
Puppet, puppet, it's a puppet!

356
00:18:04,980 --> 00:18:06,520
Here we go.

357
00:18:06,520 --> 00:18:08,480
Turn!

358
00:18:08,480 --> 00:18:10,700
Oh, the Mandalorian!

359
00:18:10,700 --> 00:18:14,300
The legendary Mandalorian.

360
00:18:14,300 --> 00:18:17,560
You know...

361
00:18:17,560 --> 00:18:19,800
The Jaba people...

362
00:18:19,800 --> 00:18:25,360
They really love those androids and Mandalorians.

363
00:18:25,360 --> 00:18:27,060
Thanks for liking them!

364
00:18:27,060 --> 00:18:27,920
Is this the one...

365
00:18:27,920 --> 00:18:32,140
The one where he's already wearing the Beskar armor?

366
00:18:32,140 --> 00:18:34,580
The Mandalorian.

367
00:18:34,580 --> 00:18:38,020
A solitary bounty hunter with top-tier skills.

368
00:18:38,020 --> 00:18:40,080
Though he's not so solitary anymore.

369
00:18:40,080 --> 00:18:42,220
He's constantly being pushed around by Grogu.

370
00:18:42,220 --> 00:18:43,860
His real name is Din Djarin.

371
00:18:43,860 --> 00:18:47,280
A lone wolf who never shows his face, following the creed.

372
00:18:47,280 --> 00:18:52,080
I think someone said, "If he shows his face, just kill him," but...

373
00:18:52,080 --> 00:18:54,680
Since when did it become that?

374
00:18:54,680 --> 00:18:57,480
Wait, when did that happen?

375
00:18:57,480 --> 00:19:00,280
Did they say that in the show? Like, "Just kill him if he does"?

376
00:19:00,280 --> 00:19:02,110
Was it actually like that?

377
00:19:02,110 --> 00:19:03,880
Should you just kill him?

378
00:19:04,880 --> 00:19:06,680
I don't think it was like that.

379
00:19:06,680 --> 00:19:09,480
Wait, I haven't gotten any duplicates yet!

380
00:19:09,480 --> 00:19:11,280
1, 2, 3, ..., 6.

381
00:19:11,280 --> 00:19:13,280
Whoa, I'm getting them all in one box!

382
00:19:13,280 --> 00:19:14,840
Maybe I didn't need to buy so many after all.

383
00:19:14,840 --> 00:19:15,940
Wait a second.

384
00:19:15,940 --> 00:19:18,560
If I can complete the set with one box, that's crazy.

385
00:19:18,560 --> 00:19:20,120
No way.

386
00:19:20,120 --> 00:19:22,900
This is wild.

387
00:19:22,900 --> 00:19:23,680
But...

388
00:19:23,680 --> 00:19:24,820
Listen...

389
00:19:24,820 --> 00:19:25,760
Wait.

390
00:19:25,760 --> 00:19:27,720
But still...

391
00:19:27,720 --> 00:19:29,260
With these things...

392
00:19:29,260 --> 00:19:31,400
You can't trade them unless you have duplicates.

393
00:19:31,400 --> 00:19:31,800
You know?

394
00:19:32,860 --> 00:19:34,820
You need the duplicates to use for trading.

395
00:19:34,820 --> 00:19:36,940
In a way, I actually want duplicates.

396
00:19:36,940 --> 00:19:39,440
Is this lucky or not?

397
00:19:39,440 --> 00:19:41,840
No duplicates so far, definitely.

398
00:19:41,840 --> 00:19:44,040
Here we go. I think I'll start getting duplicates soon.

399
00:19:44,040 --> 00:19:44,900
Pop!

400
00:19:44,900 --> 00:19:46,660
Ah, a duplicate!

401
00:19:46,660 --> 00:19:48,680
Bo-katan.

402
00:19:48,680 --> 00:19:53,730
Satine Kryze's sister, who Obi-Wan loved.

403
00:19:53,730 --> 00:19:57,570
Korone has this one scene she absolutely loves.

404
00:19:57,570 --> 00:19:59,450
You know, when Darth Maul...

405
00:19:59,450 --> 00:20:01,530
He kills Satine Kryze, right?

406
00:20:01,530 --> 00:20:04,250
I just love that scene.

407
00:20:04,250 --> 00:20:07,310
Not that I love the killing part specifically,

408
00:20:07,310 --> 00:20:10,030
but you know,

409
00:20:10,030 --> 00:20:12,590
it's not like I'm just happy she's dying.

410
00:20:12,590 --> 00:20:13,330
It's just so powerful.

411
00:20:13,330 --> 00:20:16,350
Obi-Wan and Satine...

412
00:20:16,350 --> 00:20:18,770
They're like this,

413
00:20:18,770 --> 00:20:20,250
they love each other,

414
00:20:20,250 --> 00:20:22,030
but because of their positions,

415
00:20:22,030 --> 00:20:23,370
they can't even say it,

416
00:20:23,370 --> 00:20:24,750
they can't be together,

417
00:20:24,750 --> 00:20:27,110
they just couldn't make it work, right?

418
00:20:27,110 --> 00:20:29,950
But then Darth Maul...

419
00:20:29,950 --> 00:20:31,830
And Darth Maul,

420
00:20:31,830 --> 00:20:33,830
since he hates Obi-Wan so much,

421
00:20:33,830 --> 00:20:35,090
of course he's going to kill her.

422
00:20:35,090 --> 00:20:39,310
He wants to make Obi-Wan suffer, after all.

423
00:20:39,310 --> 00:20:44,470
So, right in front of Obi-Wan, he just stabs Satine—bam!

424
00:20:44,470 --> 00:20:49,910
And as she's fading away, she tells him for the first time in Obi-Wan's arms, "I loved you."

425
00:20:49,910 --> 00:20:53,990
That scene is just... it's a real tear-jerker.

426
00:20:53,990 --> 00:20:55,530
And this is her sister.

427
00:20:55,530 --> 00:20:57,170
Right.

428
00:20:57,170 --> 00:21:00,710
A talented Mandalorian warrior.

429
00:21:00,710 --> 00:21:03,430
Wearing the armor passed down through generations,

430
00:21:03,430 --> 00:21:06,210
she continues to fight for the future of Mandalore.

431
00:21:06,210 --> 00:21:07,750


432
00:21:07,750 --> 00:21:08,130
Um, so,

433
00:21:08,130 --> 00:21:09,510
this person is like,

434
00:21:09,510 --> 00:21:11,070
"Go for it! Just do it!"

435
00:21:11,070 --> 00:21:12,990
The Mandalorians are great, but

436
00:21:12,990 --> 00:21:14,990
the older sister,

437
00:21:14,990 --> 00:21:16,390
she actually wants things to be peaceful.

438
00:21:16,390 --> 00:21:17,710
She's like, "Quiet, quiet!"

439
00:21:17,710 --> 00:21:19,930
"Let's all just get along!"

440
00:21:19,930 --> 00:21:20,750
That's kind of her vibe.

441
00:21:20,750 --> 00:21:22,770
That's how it is.

442
00:21:22,770 --> 00:21:25,810
Yeah, like that.

443
00:21:25,810 --> 00:21:27,630
Hmm.

444
00:21:27,630 --> 00:21:30,310
Well, she passed away eventually.

445
00:21:30,310 --> 00:21:31,630
Right in front of Obi-Wan.

446
00:21:31,630 --> 00:21:32,910
Actually, seriously,

447
00:21:32,910 --> 00:21:34,630
I mean, really,

448
00:21:34,630 --> 00:21:36,610
how did Obi-Wan not fall to the dark side?

449
00:21:36,610 --> 00:21:38,150
That guy is amazing.

450
00:21:38,150 --> 00:21:40,230
His mental strength is insane.

451
00:21:40,230 --> 00:21:42,310
Okay, give me a chocolate.

452
00:21:42,310 --> 00:21:45,710
Seriously.

453
00:21:45,710 --> 00:21:47,290
Pop!

454
00:21:47,290 --> 00:21:49,430
Oh, Luke Skywalker! Yay!

455
00:21:49,430 --> 00:21:50,370
Prime Luke.

456
00:21:50,370 --> 00:21:52,830
Prime Luke has appeared!

457
00:21:52,830 --> 00:21:56,210
Honestly,

458
00:21:57,010 --> 00:21:58,410
Obi-Wan is incredible.

459
00:21:58,410 --> 00:22:00,010
It really made me realize how great Obi-Wan is.

460
00:22:02,010 --> 00:22:03,210
Alright, here we go!

461
00:22:03,210 --> 00:22:04,410
They're overlapping a bit.

462
00:22:05,010 --> 00:22:05,610
Going in!

463
00:22:07,410 --> 00:22:08,410
First, let's get the chocolate out.

464
00:22:11,610 --> 00:22:15,410
Prime Luke usually starts from the end of his arc.

465
00:22:15,410 --> 00:22:17,010
Well, that's about right.

466
00:22:18,880 --> 00:22:20,080
Oh, wait, I want this one.

467
00:22:20,480 --> 00:22:21,280
Ah, this is...

468
00:22:21,480 --> 00:22:22,280
The Armorer, right?

469
00:22:22,680 --> 00:22:24,100
The Armorer!

470
00:22:28,570 --> 00:22:32,890
The woman who crafts Mandalorian armor.

471
00:22:32,890 --> 00:22:35,090
She has a workshop in a hidden forge on Nevarro.

472
00:22:35,090 --> 00:22:37,110
She cherishes the Code

473
00:22:37,110 --> 00:22:38,430
that Mandalorians must follow.

474
00:22:38,430 --> 00:22:39,810
The Armorer.

475
00:22:39,810 --> 00:22:42,270
You're really something, seriously.

476
00:22:42,270 --> 00:22:45,050
The Armorer keeps saying "This is the Way."

477
00:22:45,050 --> 00:22:46,550
Well, she doesn't exactly repeat it constantly,

478
00:22:46,550 --> 00:22:47,230
but it's like,

479
00:22:47,230 --> 00:22:50,890
"If I just say 'This is the Way,' it'll cover everything," kind of vibe.

480
00:22:50,890 --> 00:22:53,330
Yeah, that's why I love the Armorer.

481
00:22:53,330 --> 00:22:55,730
Our way.

482
00:22:55,730 --> 00:22:58,390
If we just make a little 'Mandalorian IF' scenario...

483
00:22:58,390 --> 00:22:59,630
Our way.

484
00:22:59,630 --> 00:23:03,050
They say that a lot, and I love it.

485
00:23:03,050 --> 00:23:06,750
I really like that.

486
00:23:06,750 --> 00:23:09,070
Alright, moving on.

487
00:23:09,070 --> 00:23:11,150
Feels like I'll collect them all pretty quickly.

488
00:23:11,150 --> 00:23:14,950
Here we go.

489
00:23:14,950 --> 00:23:16,430
Turn!

490
00:23:32,430 --> 00:23:42,430
Equipped with custom Mandalorian armor and wielding high-lethality weapons...

491
00:23:44,140 --> 00:23:48,940
A taciturn bounty hunter. After building an extensive career, he became a legend.

492
00:23:48,940 --> 00:23:52,420
And he is loved by Inugami Korone!

493
00:23:52,420 --> 00:23:53,800
Like, 'A-ha!'

494
00:23:53,800 --> 00:23:56,280
A-ha! He's here, Boba Fett! Yay!

495
00:23:56,280 --> 00:23:57,260
Look at Boba-chan!

496
00:23:57,260 --> 00:23:59,720
Oh, it's Boba.

497
00:23:59,720 --> 00:24:00,880
Did you get Boba?

498
00:24:01,100 --> 00:24:02,600
Yeah, I got Boba Fett!

499
00:24:02,600 --> 00:24:03,960
Can I have this one?

500
00:24:04,220 --> 00:24:08,380
But we're streaming right now, so if we don't keep it here, we won't know what we've collected, right?

501
00:24:08,380 --> 00:24:09,880
Got it. Can you give it to me later?

502
00:24:10,140 --> 00:24:10,640
Sure.

503
00:24:10,640 --> 00:24:11,980
Then I'll wait over there.

504
00:24:11,980 --> 00:24:18,080
I'm gonna get killed if Boba Fett sees this.

505
00:24:18,080 --> 00:24:22,980
Boba Fett will definitely kill me for this.

506
00:24:22,980 --> 00:24:25,020
Well, I wonder about the current Boba Fett.

507
00:24:25,020 --> 00:24:27,360
He probably wouldn't even bother.

508
00:24:27,360 --> 00:24:30,420
Yeah, he probably wouldn't.

509
00:24:33,450 --> 00:24:37,730
Like, 'Oh, there's another crazy one,' kind of vibe.

510
00:24:37,730 --> 00:24:42,790
And Fennec would be like, 'Should I kill them?'

511
00:24:42,790 --> 00:24:45,430
Alright, next one.

512
00:24:45,430 --> 00:24:46,530
Turn!

513
00:24:46,530 --> 00:24:48,010
Ah! A Dark Trooper!

514
00:24:48,010 --> 00:24:51,230
See, I didn't know this, but about Dark Troopers...

515
00:24:51,230 --> 00:24:54,110
They appeared in a game first, right?

516
00:24:54,110 --> 00:24:59,120
The veteran Star Wars fans were making a huge deal about the Dark Troopers.

517
00:24:59,120 --> 00:25:08,810
Like, they were so happy because they'd only seen them in games until now. Apparently, their first appearance was in a game.

518
00:25:08,810 --> 00:25:18,810
Discarding the humanity of the interior for the evolution of a complete combat droid, the third-generation Dark Trooper. An extremely terrifying and dangerous entity.

519
00:25:21,070 --> 00:25:24,350
The game really did come first.

520
00:25:24,510 --> 00:25:30,650
No duplicates yet! We're doing good. I brought a bunch of heavy stuff over here...

521
00:25:30,650 --> 00:25:37,920
Hey, weren't they improved?

522
00:25:37,920 --> 00:25:39,780
The... Mofugileon?

523
00:25:39,780 --> 00:25:42,340
This is probably because...

524
00:25:42,340 --> 00:25:45,600
It's armor made of Beskar.

525
00:25:45,600 --> 00:25:50,120
That's why it's so strong. The Mandalorians were almost unstoppable.

526
00:25:50,120 --> 00:25:57,180
But if it went up against Luke Skywalker in his prime...

527
00:25:57,180 --> 00:25:58,180
Actually...

528
00:25:58,180 --> 00:26:02,800
That scene where Luke beats the Dark Trooper...

529
00:26:02,800 --> 00:26:04,220
How should I put it...

530
00:26:04,220 --> 00:26:06,100
It was so quick and effortless.

531
00:26:06,100 --> 00:26:08,940
It really made me realize how strong he is.

532
00:26:08,940 --> 00:26:10,640
Seriously.

533
00:26:10,640 --> 00:26:13,280
Jedi are terrifying, aren't they?

534
00:26:13,280 --> 00:26:14,520
They really are scary.

535
00:26:14,520 --> 00:26:16,340
Seriously.

536
00:26:16,340 --> 00:26:18,480
Really.

537
00:26:18,480 --> 00:26:20,020
And if you make one little mistake...

538
00:26:20,020 --> 00:26:22,400
You fall to the dark side, right?

539
00:26:22,400 --> 00:26:23,880
It's scary.

540
00:26:23,880 --> 00:26:25,380
Truly.

541
00:26:25,380 --> 00:26:26,640
And also, that...

542
00:26:26,640 --> 00:26:28,260
The very beginning part...

543
00:26:28,260 --> 00:26:29,820
Um...

544
00:26:29,820 --> 00:26:33,460
